    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c0edc53d_6c0e116e",
        "filename": "drivers/scsi/ufs/ufshcd-crypto.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-14T23:19:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The key size validation is broken, as this allows e.g. 64 bytes for AES-CBC.  AES-512 does not exist :-)  I think it would be easiest to just whitelist the allowed sizes for each algorithm.  AES-XTS allows 32, 48, 64; the others allow 16 and 32.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "47f21f1bf010b47f228ca4d8925bce4290dcf0c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e435c82_506bb5b2",
        "filename": "drivers/scsi/ufs/ufshcd-crypto.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1368904
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-27T22:16:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure how legit this is, but: https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/6122835 :P\n\nBut anyway, the reason I let 64 bytes go through is because the UFS spec defines a keysize for 512 bits, but none of the algorithms explicitly specified by UFS use it (as opposed to the other keysizes where some non-zero subset of algorithms use keys of that size), and I figured the 64 byte key layout is a natural extension from everything else, and in any case, a 64 byte key wouldn\u0027t be programmed anyway unless there is a crypto capability with a 64 byte key. But thinking about it more, I should probably be consistent and either allow all combinations of keysize+algs or allow only those specified explicitly in the spec - I\u0027m leaning towards keeping this function as purely something that formats a key properly, and has no knowledge of what keysizes are allowed with which crypto algs. In any case, the key_size_bytes input argument is also useless and only causing issues (it was originally there as the key buffer\u0027s size, which became pointless after I started passing in the cap_idx), so I\u0027ve removed the whole deal with key_size_bytes.",
      "parentUuid": "c0edc53d_6c0e116e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 119,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "47f21f1bf010b47f228ca4d8925bce4290dcf0c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "63c74220_6cd13108",
        "filename": "drivers/scsi/ufs/ufshcd-crypto.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 132,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-14T23:19:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is redundant because if there\u0027s no crypto support, then num_crypto_cap \u003d\u003d 0 so then by definition the capability index will be invalid.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 132,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 132,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "47f21f1bf010b47f228ca4d8925bce4290dcf0c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1fd3087a_df30544f",
        "filename": "drivers/scsi/ufs/ufshcd-crypto.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 132,
      "author": {
        "id": 1368904
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-27T22:16:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ufshcd_is_crypto_enabled is different from ufshcd_hba_is_crypto_supported, so this isn\u0027t redundant.\n\nThat said, ufshcd_is_crypto_enabled isn\u0027t currently called by any function after initialization, so right now after all initialization, ufshcd_is_crypto_enabled should return the same thing as ufshcd_hba_is_crypto_supported, but maybe we should expose ufshcd_crypto_enable/disable to userspace (or if we think that\u0027s not worthwhile, just get rid of the function)?",
      "parentUuid": "63c74220_6cd13108",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 132,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 132,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "47f21f1bf010b47f228ca4d8925bce4290dcf0c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
